  "_meta": {
      "purpose": "A fixed set of buyer-language queries, kept in the repository so accuracy figures can be re-run after any change. Earlier spot checks (30 and 28 fresh products, 11 multilingual queries) were never saved, so their figures could not be reproduced.",
      "written": "2026-10-04",
      "expect": "Each query lists the standards that answer it, by number and part without edition. A result answers it when its number, edition removed, is one of them, or a part of one listed without a part ('IS 16102' accepts 'IS 16102 (Part 1)'). Every expected standard was checked against the corpus title before it was listed.",
      "languages": "The non-English queries are the same everyday items in each of 12 Indian languages, written to read as a buyer would type them. They have not been reviewed by native speakers; a phrase found unnatural should be corrected here and the figures re-run, not tuned around.",
      "not_tuned_on": "Written before any was run. Fixes informed by a miss must not be judged on the query that informed them alone.",
      "label_changes": "Widened after the first run (2026-10-04), where the engine's answer is a current standard for the words of the query as written: 'steel rods/bars for concrete' without 'high strength' or 'TMT' also accepts IS 432 (Part 1), mild steel bars for concrete reinforcement (all languages except Hindi, whose query says high strength); 'flush door shutters solid core' accepts either part of IS 2202, both solid core; 'packaged drinking water bottles' also accepts IS 15410, the bottles themselves. Not widened: a superseded edition ranked first (IS 13849 for the ABC extinguisher) is a miss. The baseline figures quoted in PROGRESS.md are recomputed with these labels."
  },
